    "The main topic of the guideline is the management of Atrial Fibrillation (AF) with a focus on pharmacological cardioversion as an alternative or in conjunction with electrical cardioversion. Several recommendations and supporting studies are outlined regarding specific pharmacological agents and their application based on patient conditions such as hemodynamic stability and left ventricular function. Specific mentions of drugs include ibutilide, amiodarone, flecainide, propafenone, and procainamide. The document highlights the effectiveness and considerations for these treatments, including side effects and patient contraindications such as prolonged QT interval and existing heart conditions like heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF).": "genes",
